json scores the same forecasts at independent ASOS rain gauges.", "ETS can be raised by forecasting rain too often: the frequency bias (1 = right number of rain days) is shown next to every ETS, and the 'same correction for all' view quantile-maps every model's amounts the same way before scoring.", "rainfallAI, the statistical baseline and NBM are post-processed with observations; the other rows are raw model output. rainfallAI also uses GFS, GEFS, NBM, HRRR, IFS and ENS forecasts as inputs. group_rank compares single runs, ensemble means and post-processed products among themselves.", "ERA5-start rows (FuXi, Atlas) are a best-case reference (ERA5 is not available in real time and uses observations from after the start); they are not ranked. FuXi and Atlas started from the IFS analysis are ranked once all 38 starts are done.", "GEFS and ECMWF ENS are ensemble means: smooth fields that rain lightly in many places, which lowers MAE but costs ETS at the heavier thresholds.", "rainfallAI here is the fixed ens_v5d model with the hzlead amount rule (test look #6), not the newer live version.", "rainfallAI, stack v2 (statistical baseline): version chosen after scores on this same period were seen (several test looks), so these numbers are optimistic; the clean comparison is the forward table from the 2026-11-09 cycle (rainfallAI frozen 2026-11-08).", "Climatology = the 2021-2025 MRMS average for the same calendar window (valid day +-15 days) in each 0.1 deg cell (cells outside the MRMS data area filled from the nearest cell; imputation mask in rainfallAI/data/refs/imputed/); in the probability tables its probabilities (share of those 155 days reaching each amount) are the reference of the Brier skill score, so climatology scores 0 and above 0 means better than climatology (at gauges: the gauge's cell). Reference rows are shown, never ranked, and do not shape the common sample.", "Persistence = the observed MRMS (Pass 2) 24 h total ending at the start, repeated for all 7 days (probabilities from the same 1.1 deg neighbourhood as the single runs); it is published about 2 h after the start. An analysis-based reference, not an operational forecast product. Reference rows are shown, never ranked, and do not shape the common sample."], "policy": "Rows whose start is not available in real time (ERA5, which assimilates observations from after the start, or IFS starts with same-day OISST sea temperature / ERA5 clouds) are shown as an unranked reference; ranked rows share one sample; group_rank = rank within single runs / ensemble means / post-processed products", "group_labels": {"single": "single runs (raw)", "ensmean": "ensemble means (raw)", "postproc": "post-processed on observations", "reference": "reference: start not available in real time (ERA5, or same-day OISST / ERA5 clouds; unranked)"}, "ci_block_sensitivity": {"block_starts": [1, 2, 4, 8], "median_ci_width": [0.0374, 0.0479, 0.0617, 0.0702], "rank_range": {"aifs": [[2, 3], [2, 3], [2, 3], [2, 3]], "aigfs": [[6, 7], [5, 7], [5, 7], [5, 7]], "cesm": [[15, 15], [15, 15], [15, 15], [15, 15]], "e3sm": [[16, 16], [16, 16], [16, 16], [16, 16]], "gefs": [[8, 11], [8, 11], [8, 11], [8, 11]], "gfs": [[11, 13], [11, 13], [10, 13], [10, 13]], "graphcast_ifs": [[3, 4], [3, 4], [3, 4], [3, 4]], "icon": [[11, 13], [11, 13], [11, 13], [11, 13]], "ifs": [[6, 7], [6, 7], [6, 7], [6, 7]], "ifs_ens": [[5, 5], [5, 6], [5, 6], [5, 6]], "mpas": [[14, 14], [14, 14], [14, 14], [14, 14]], "nbm": [[8, 11], [8, 12], [9, 12], [9, 12]], "rainai": [[1, 1], [1, 1], [1, 1], [1, 1]], "stack": [[2, 4], [2, 4], [2, 4], [2, 4]], "ukmo": [[8, 11], [8, 11], [8, 11], [8, 11]], "wrf": [[8, 13], [8, 13], [8, 13], [8, 13]]}, "p_top": {"aifs": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "aigfs": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "cesm": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "e3sm": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "gefs": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "gfs": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "graphcast_ifs": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "icon": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "ifs": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "ifs_ens": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "mpas": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "nbm": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "rainai": [1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0], "stack": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "ukmo": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "wrf": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]}}, "rank_metric": "ets01", "corrected_method": "same correction for all: each model's daily totals (rainfallAI included) are quantile-mapped, per lead day and pooled over the US, to the distribution of the truth used in this table, fitted leave-one-month-out (July, August, September, October starts); dry stays dry. Afterwards every model's rain frequency is much closer to the truth's, so ETS depends mostly on where the rain is placed; some frequency differences remain (dry forecasts stay dry, limited samples, month-to-month shifts). Retrospective cross-validation sensitivity (other months include later ones), not a deployable calibration.", "ci_method": "95 % intervals from a moving-block bootstrap over the 38 start dates: 1,000 resamples (fixed seed), each made of blocks of 4 consecutive starts (12 days; neighbouring starts overlap in time and share weather), each start kept whole (its full map or station set and all 7 lead days); ETS >= 0.1 in (mean over lead days 1-7, each day from the summed hit, false-alarm and miss counts) is recomputed in every resample on the same common sample. rank_range = 2.5-97.5 % range of a model's rank among the ranked models, p_top = share of resamples in which it ranks first. The 'same correction for all' values are reused in the resamples, not refitted. The block length is a choice: fair.ci_block_sensitivity repeats the as-run intervals and rank ranges with blocks of 1, 2, 4 and 8 starts.", "ci_resamples": 1000, "ci_seed": 20261109}}